@@ -311,7 +311,7 @@
           "source_section": "Statement",
           "quote": "Assume dependent choice, as available under the Axiom of Choice. Let $R$ be a commutative ring. The following are equivalent.\n\n1. $R$ is Noetherian ([[def-noetherian-ring]]).\n2. Every ideal of $R$ is finitely generated: for every ideal $\\mathfrak a$ there\n   are finitely many $a_1,\\ldots,a_n\\in\\mathfrak a$, with $n\\in\\mathbb N$, such\n   that $\\mathfrak a=(a_1,\\ldots,a_n)$.\n3. **Ascending chain condition.** Every chain of ideals\n   $\\mathfrak a_0\\subseteq\\mathfrak a_1\\subseteq\\mathfrak a_2\\subseteq\\cdots$\n   indexed by $\\mathbb N$ stabilises: there is $N\\in\\mathbb N$ with\n   $\\mathfrak a_n=\\mathfrak a_N$ for every $n\\ge N$.\n4. **Maximal condition.** Every nonempty set of ideals of $R$ has a maximal\n   member with respect to inclusion.\n\nThe implication $3\\Rightarrow4$ uses dependent choice. The implications\n$1\\Leftrightarrow2$, $2\\Rightarrow3$, and $4\\Rightarrow2$ are choice-free. The same\nattribution is carried by\n[[thm-equivalent-characterizations-of-noetherian-modules]], from which this\nstatement is obtained.\n\n",
           "uses": [
-            "1.2"
+            "2.1"
           ]
